{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1793550000000-architect-module-pins-review.report.md'","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-16 06:06:47 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-16 13:06:47 +07\nCoding-Agent: claude (claude-fable-5-1)\nSession-ID: pending\nRole: Architect (read-only; worktree datomworld-srvm-pins, branch srvm-module-pins @ 6df441d0, 13 uncommitted files)\nBrief: collab/1793540000000-architect-module-pins-review.prompt.md\nInputs: collab/1792130530811-engineer-module-pins.report.md, collab/1793520000000-architect-fetch-threat-model.report.md (§4.2, §4.4, §6), the full `git diff`, and the sources cited below.\n\n# Module pins: Part A review of R4, Part B ruling on host-module pins, Part C round-2 steps\n\n## Part A: review of the uncommitted R4 part\n\n### A.0 What was checked\n\n- Gate placement: `check-install-admission!` (`rows.cljc:1883-1892`) runs in `lower-task` after `check-custody!` and before `attach-streams!` (`rows.cljc:2301-2304`), over every task of `task-tree` (`rows.cljc:1805-1808`, root and every nested install child, pre-order). Refusal throws before the first attach: the attach-count law holds (tests assert zero attaches).\n- Paths that lower install children: only `rows/lower-task`. Backends (`layout/lower-task`) refuse `:installs` already; `remote.cljc:485` lowers no installs; fork packs go through the same `lower-task`; `holder.export/rehydrate-fenced` now forwards `:yin.k/admitted` (`export.cljc:539`); the holder driver's two lower paths are discussed in P2-1.\n- Other copies of the sender's admission: `engine/link-install` (`engine.cljc:1436-1443`) is the only consumer of the four `:yin.admit/*` response fields outside the linker; nothing else reads the installed entry's `:admission` (grep over `src`: only `linker/admission.cljc`, `linker/interpreter.cljc`, `yin.repl` configuration, none read `(:admission entry)`). Dropping rather than replacing is safe for consumers.\n- Refusal shape: `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {name carried-address}}}` matches threat-model §4.4 exactly (no `:yin.k/kind`, no `:yin.k/discovery`). The carried address can never be nil at this point because `check-install!` already required a manifest map (`rows.cljc:1846-1851`), so `{'host.mod nil}` in the admitted map correctly refuses.\n- Mutants: all three are meaningful (name-only acceptance, retained sender admission, gate bypass) and each is killed by distinct assertions. Mutant 2 has to be re-done after P1-1 (see below).\n- Tests: portable (plain data, keyword sentinel addresses, host-neutral catch forms, kondo clean per the engineer). Fixtures admit their fixed manifests explicitly from the composition side (`rows_support.cljc:298-301`, `safepoint_harness_test.cljc:349-352`), never derived from the pack.\n- Docs: continuation §2.5 and §7.1 (\"the lower does not re-discharge free names\") are unchanged and still true, since the pin work has not landed. UCF §7.6.4/§7.6.5 are unchanged spec text. The §7.11 row, continuation Q5, revisions I-8 and the known-gaps rows say \"blocked\" for the pin carrier: no overclaim. The claims that are wrong after P1-1 are listed under P3-3.\n\n### A.1 Findings\n\n**P1-1. Dropping the sender's admission at restore breaks fenced recovery and the relift law for every real pack with an install child.**\nThe lift copies the install record's `response` whole into the `:install` row (`install-node`, `rows.cljc:1643`). The linker's interpreter puts `:yin.admit/id`, `:yin.admit/decision`, `:yin.admit/asserters` and `:yin.admit/address` on every successful DHT-admitted response (`interpreter.cljc:416-421`), so a real pack's `:install` row carries them. The new restore-side `dissoc` (`rows.cljc:2236-2237`) then produces a machine whose `:installs` response lacks the four keys. Consequences:\n- `rehydrate-fenced` re-prepares and re-encodes the restored machine and demands byte equality with the published pack (`export.cljc:548-556`); the relift's install row now differs from the carried one, so every fenced recovery of such a pack answers `:yin.k/undecodable :recovery-inconsistent`.\n- The harness law \"the relift equals the lift by root\" (`safepoint_harness_test.cljc:10`, asserted at `:629` via `canonical-under`) fails for the same packs.\nThe current tests pass only because every fixture response (`rows_support/module-response`, `blocking-body`) carries no `:yin.admit/*` keys. This is a correctness defect, not a test gap.\nRequired fix (revert-not-fix does not apply, this is the slice's own line): strip the four `:yin.admit/*` keys **at lift**, in `install-node`, so the pack never carries S's decision (\"the carrier narrows, never widens\", §4.1), and make the lower **refuse** a carried response that still carries any `:yin.admit/*` key as `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response` (one clause in `check-install!`'s existing `and`; hand-crafted packs only). Delete the restore-side `dissoc`. Then the restored response equals the carried one, fenced reproduction and the relift law hold by construction, and `link-install` sees no sender record. New pin for the mutant: a source whose install response carries the record lifts to an `:install` row without the keys (assert on the decoded row's slot 3), and a pack with the keys spliced back in is refused before attach with zero attaches. Keep the existing \"installed entry has no `:admission`\" assertion.\n\n**P2-1. The holder driver has no seam to supply `:yin.k/admitted`, so the composition's real lower path refuses every pack with an install child.**\n`driver/lowered` is called with `{:exclusive true}` (`driver.cljc:2294`) and with the grant map (`driver.cljc:1588-1600`); the fenced recovery at `driver.cljc:2455-2457` passes only `:address` and `:attach`. None forwards an admitted map. This is fail-closed (safe) but it means R4 as written makes carried install children unreachable through the holder, with no driver test noticing (`driver_test.cljc` has no install-child handoff; `:2726` fakes one for gate-mode only). Required for round 2, not for landing R4 alone: a config entry `(:yin.k/admitted-modules (:config state))` forwarded by `lowered` and by the fenced recovery call (two lines), plus one driver test that lowers a parked-installer checkpoint with and without the config. Until then, a known-gaps row \"holder driver passes no admitted-modules map; install-child handoff through the driver refuses\" (P2) must land with R4.\n\n**P2-2. `:yin.k/admitted` already means two other things in the same vocabulary.**\nIt is a ledger fact kind, \"one effect's dedup record with its result\" (`ledger.cljc:22, 115, 553`), and the driver's not-holder answer field for the admitted variant set (`driver.cljc:743, 1655`). The threat model (§4.4, my text) chose the word carelessly. Rename the lower option to `:yin.k/admitted-modules` in `rows.cljc`, `export.cljc`, the five test files and the five doc amendments. Cheap now, a permanent vocabulary defect after commit.\n\n**P3-1. The gate reports one child, not the complete set, and omits `:yin.k/discovery`.**\nEvery other `:yin.k/unsatisfied` from the lower carries `:yin.k/discovery` (`rows.cljc:1629, 1686, 1923, 1930`). §4.4's shape omitted it; §4.2's has `:complete`. Ruling: in round 2 fold the admission gate into the single `check-modules!` stage (Part C step 5), which collects every unlisted child of the tree and every unsatisfied pin into one `:yin.k/missing` map with `:yin.k/discovery :complete`. Not blocking for landing R4 alone; the §4.4 shape is acceptable until then.\n\n**P3-2. Name-keyed admission across the tree.** The admitted map is flat by module name over the whole tree. A nested child that installs the same name as a sibling at another address cannot be admitted. The registry family makes this a degenerate case; note it in the `lower-task` docstring, no code.\n\n**P3-3. Doc statements to retarget after P1-1.** Continuation §7.2 amendment (\"Restore drops the sender's …\"), Q3 amendment (\"drops the sender's admission evidence on restore\"), `yin.vm.linker.dht.md:2333-2335`, transport-tuples amendment (\"Restore drops the sender's four …\"), revisions I-8 (\"restore drops\"), known-gaps R4 row (\"sender admission dropped on restore\"). All become \"the lift never carries the sender's admission fields; a carried one is `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response`\". Also replace `:yin.k/admitted` by the P2-2 name in all five docs.\n\n**P3-4. `holder.export/rehydrate-fenced` docstring** says \"default empty\" twice in different words; fine. No change needed.\n\nVerdict for Part A: **CHANGES-REQUIRED** (P1-1 blocking; P2-2 rename and the P2-1 ledger row land with it; P3-1/P3-2 deferred to round 2).\n\n## Part B: ruling on host-module (\"nil\") pins\n\n### B.0 Facts the ruling rests on\n\n- A host-registered entry has `:address nil` and lists its exports as `:yin.module/primitives {sym profile-address}` (`register-host-module`, `module.cljc:223-263`). `module/host-export-profile` answers exactly that profile address for a qualified symbol (`module.cljc:266-281`): a **keyword** `:yin.k.pp/blake3-…` minted by `vm/primitive-profile` over `{name class arities effects host-state}` (`vm.cljc:338-356`). Plain data, no functions, no host objects. The core `stream` and `cell` modules are host modules with literal cljc profiles and `:none` host-state (`module.cljc:350-363, 405-410`), so their addresses are identical on JVM, Node and Dart.\n- The linker already defines \"satisfied by equal profile\" for exactly this case: `declared-discharge` discharges a primitive obligation by `(= profile (module/host-export-profile modules name))` (`linker.cljc:1014-1018`), and a module obligation by equal manifest address (`:1022-1027`). UCF §7.6.5 already carries `:yin.k/primitives {name <expected profile>}` in the outcome.\n- The lift's `discharge!` answers a qualified free name by registry presence (`rows.cljc:1611-1616`) and nothing of the entry travels. The task row's `requires` slot is a plain map (`rows.cljc:1687-1689`), so two more keys cost no slot change.\n\n### B.1 Ruling\n\n1. **Host modules participate in this slice.** Not deferred. Reason: `stream` and `cell`, the most common modules in any pack, are host modules; deferring leaves R6 (silent skew) open for the common case while closing it only for DHT-linked modules. The data is already pure, the comparison already exists in the linker, and the lift already resolves the entry. The risk of implementing is one more `requires` key and a fixture re-mint, both owed anyway for `:yin.k/modules`. The risk of deferring is a second re-mint later and a documented hole in the fetch-loop contract.\n\n2. **What the lift records.** Only what the live code uses: for every live free name `ns/f` that `discharge!` answered through the registry (`rows.cljc:1614-1616`, after `E`, store, primitives and installing names, which stay as they are):\n   - `:yin.k/modules` gets `{ns <manifest address>}` when the entry is linked (`(:address entry)` non-nil), `{ns nil}` when it is host-registered;\n   - `:yin.k/host-exports` gets `{ns/f <profile address>}` when the entry is host-registered, the value being `(module/host-export-profile (:modules m) 'ns/f)`.\n   Not all exports. Recording all exports would refuse a receiver whose host module gained or changed an export the code never touches, and it would persist what the free-name scan already derives. A lift where `host-export-profile` answers nil for a name the registry claims to hold (an entry with a malformed `:yin.module/primitives`) is `:yin.k/non-portable :host-export-profile {:yin.k/name ns/f}`.\n\n3. **Canonical encoding.** Two maps in the task row's `requires` beside `:yin.k/segments`, `:yin.k/trees` and `:yin.k/cursor-profiles`: `:yin.k/modules {symbol -> string-or-nil}` and `:yin.k/host-exports {qualified-symbol -> keyword}`. Keys sorted by the carrier's existing rules for symbol keys; the `keyed`/`built` host-collapse discipline applies (module names contain dots, no slash; a qualified export has one slash, so the known P3 `keyed` gap does not reach these maps, but add the count guard anyway as the `built` precedent). Absent maps are not emitted when empty (same as `:yin.k/trees` with no segments is still emitted; follow whatever the existing `requires` does for empties, byte-stable). No richer value in `:yin.k/modules`: a tagged vector `[:host profiles]` beside address strings mixes value kinds in one slot and duplicates the primitives precedent for no gain.\n\n4. **How the lower compares** (new `check-modules!`, one pass over the whole tree, after `check-custody!`, before `attach-streams!`, absorbing today's `check-install-admission!`):\n   - `:yin.k/modules {ns address}`: receiver's `module/resolve-module` entry exists with `(= address (:address entry))` → satisfied. Entry exists with another address (including a host entry, nil, where a linked one was pinned, or vice versa) → **terminal** `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/kind :module-pin-mismatch :yin.k/name ns :yin.k/pinned address :yin.k/linked (:address entry)}`, the `:dependency-pin-mismatch` words (`engine.cljc:1388-1393`). Entry absent → collected into `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {ns address}}`.\n   - `:yin.k/host-exports {ns/f profile}`: `(= profile (module/host-export-profile (:modules recv) 'ns/f))` → satisfied. Receiver answers another profile → **terminal** `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/kind :host-export-mismatch :yin.k/name ns/f :yin.k/pinned profile :yin.k/held <receiver's>}`. Receiver answers nil (no such export, or the module is absent, or it is linked rather than host) → collected into `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/host-exports {ns/f profile}}` (the `:yin.k/modules {ns nil}` entry will be in the same map when the module is absent).\n   - Receiver's host module exporting **more** than the pin names: satisfied (subset by construction, since only used exports are pinned). Equality is of profile addresses, never of normalised profile maps: the address already covers name, class, arities, effects and host-state.\n   - Carried install children: `:yin.k/admitted-modules {ns address}` equality as today; unlisted → collected into `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {ns carried-address}}`.\n   - Order: terminal mismatches are thrown first (nothing the composition can fetch repairs them), then one collected refusal `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/discovery :complete :yin.k/missing {…}}` with keys present only where something is missing. Zero attaches in every case.\n   - The fetch loop (composition, not this slice) requires only keys of `:yin.k/missing :yin.k/modules` whose pin is non-nil; a nil pin and every `:yin.k/host-exports` entry are composition prerequisites and are not fetched.\n\n5. **Determinism across hosts.** Profile addresses are BLAKE3 content hashes over plain data computed identically on all three hosts (the same mechanism Stage E already pins for primitives); manifest addresses are segment keys. The refusal maps are plain data. Pin T8 in `stage_e_rows_test.cljc`: a `requires` with both maps re-encodes byte-identically and the two terminal refusals and the collected refusal are `=` across JVM, Node and Dart.\n\n6. **Threat-model text amended by this ruling.** §4.2's shape gains `:yin.k/host-exports`; \"whose export profiles equal those the lift recorded\" becomes \"whose profile address for each used export equals the pinned one\"; §4.4's option is renamed `:yin.k/admitted-modules` and its refusal is folded into the collected shape with `:yin.k/discovery :complete`. T4 reads: a nil pin plus `:yin.k/host-exports` is satisfied by a host module answering equal profile addresses for the pinned exports; another profile for a pinned export refuses `:host-export-mismatch`; a missing export is collected as missing; extra exports are ignored.\n\n### B.2 Alternative considered and rejected\n\n\"Refuse nothing for nil pins, document, defer\": `:yin.k/modules {ns nil}` would then only assert \"a host module of this name must exist\", which `resolve-var` already enforces at run time, and skew in `stream`/`cell` profiles between two compositions would still run under R's authority (R6, R8 for the common case). The saving is one map and one lift line; not worth a second re-mint. Rejected.\n\n## Part C: ordered steps for codex round 2\n\nPreconditions: worktree `datomworld-srvm-pins`, the current 13 files uncommitted. `npm ci` and `mise trust` are done there. Per-iteration verification is `bb test:clj`; full three-host `bb test` once at the end, one lane set at a time, foreground only. Read `docs/agents/build-n-test.md` first. No `collab/` path is ever staged.\n\n**Commit 1 (R4, lands alone): fix P1-1, rename P2-2, ledger P2-1.**\n1. `rows.cljc` `install-node`: `response` → `(dissoc response :yin.admit/id :yin.admit/decision :yin.admit/asserters :yin.admit/address)` before the `cbor/encode` check and the row. Delete the restore-side `dissoc` (`rows.cljc:2233-2237` and its comment).\n2. `rows.cljc` `check-install!`: add to the existing `and` of the `:install-response` clause `(not-any? #(= \"yin.admit\" (namespace %)) (filter keyword? (keys response)))`.\n3. Rename `:yin.k/admitted` → `:yin.k/admitted-modules` in `rows.cljc`, `export.cljc`, `rows_support.cljc`, `rows_test.cljc`, `rows_custody_test.cljc`, `export_test.cljc`, `safepoint_harness_test.cljc`.\n4. Tests in `rows_test.cljc` `carried-install-requires-receiver-admission`: keep every assertion; add (a) the decoded wire's root `:install` row slot 3 has none of the four keys, (b) the harness-style relift of the lowered machine is `=` by root to the wire (reuse `canonical-under` or compare the install row), (c) a pack with the four keys spliced into the install row refuses `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response` with zero attaches. In `export_test.cljc`: a frozen parked-installer whose source response carried the sender record rehydrates `:ok` and reproduces the pack byte for byte (this is the P1-1 regression pin).\n5. Mutants (run, record counts, restore): (m1) lift keeps the sender keys → 4(a), 4(b)/export pin fail; (m2) `check-install!` accepts `:yin.admit/*` keys → 4(c) fails; (m3) gate bypass → as before.\n6. Docs (P3-3 list): reword \"dropped on restore\" to \"never carried by the lift; a carried one is refused\", rename the option, add the known-gaps row for P2-1 (holder driver seam, P2) and the P3-2 docstring note. Revisions I-8 wording likewise.\n7. `bb test:clj`, kondo on changed files, `git diff --check`. Report; Architect sign-off; commit `fix(yin.vm.ucf): carried install children need receiver admission; lift never carries sender admission` (format.md convention, no Co-Authored-By).\n\n**Commit 2 (pins carrier + lift + lower + driver seam): the ruling.**\n8. `rows.cljc` lift: in `discharge!` (or a sibling collector over the same `answered?` walk), record for every live registry-answered name the entry: linked → `:yin.k/modules {ns address}`; host → `:yin.k/modules {ns nil}` and `:yin.k/host-exports {ns/f profile}`; nil profile → `:yin.k/non-portable :host-export-profile`. Put both maps into `requires` (`rows.cljc:1687-1689`), sorted, empty maps handled as the existing `requires` keys handle empties.\n9. Encoder/decoder/validator: `requires` is a plain map today, so confirm `check-dependencies!` (`rows.cljc:1918`) still accepts the two extra keys and add the key-count guard for symbol keys as in `built`. Malformed-slot collection: non-map `:yin.k/modules`, non-symbol key, non-string-non-nil value, non-keyword `:yin.k/host-exports` value, unqualified `:yin.k/host-exports` key → `:yin.k/undecodable :requires` (extend the existing kind, no new kind).\n10. `rows.cljc` lower: replace `check-install-admission!` by `check-modules!` per B.1 item 4 (terminal mismatches first, then one collected refusal with `:yin.k/discovery :complete`, zero attaches), same position (after custody, before attach). Delete `check-install-admission!`.\n11. Driver seam (P2-1): `driver/lowered` and the fenced recovery call forward `(:yin.k/admitted-modules (:config state))`; `rehydrate-fenced` already forwards. One driver test with and without the config over a parked-installer checkpoint.\n12. Tests (threat model §7.1, amended): T1 (lift of harness row 17 emits `{:yin.k/modules {host.mod nil} :yin.k/host-exports {host.mod/f <profile>}}`; a DHT-linked fixture emits `{pym.k <address>}`; names answered by `E`, store, prims or module stores emit nothing), T2 (receiver lacking the module: collected refusal, `:discovery :complete`, zero attaches), T3 (linked module at another address: `:module-pin-mismatch` naming both; equal address lowers), T4 (B.1 item 6), T5 (already in commit 1, re-point to the collected shape), T8 (Stage E cross-host row), T9 (layering: `rows.cljc` requires neither `linker.interpreter`, `linker.dht` nor `dao.lease`), T10 (`resolve-var` unchanged). T6/T7 (fetch loop, lease) are composition work, out of this slice; leave their known-gaps rows.\n13. Mutants (run, record, restore): lift records all exports instead of used; lower compares by name presence instead of address; lower accepts a different profile address; lower reports `:incomplete`; attach before `check-modules!`. Each must be killed by a named test.\n14. Fixture re-mint: `rows-checkpoint-v3.txt` and any ledger/Stage E fixture whose `requires` now carries the two maps; record old → new addresses in the report and in `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md` (I-8 completes, dated). C4 scanner pins are untouched (AST-level; see the standing note).\n15. Docs: continuation §2.5 (binding fact travels: the two maps), §7.1 step 6 (records address or host profile), §7.2 dependencies row (module check, three refusal kinds, delete \"the lower does not re-discharge\"), §11 Q5 closed as C with the host-export ruling, Q3 (admitted set is `:yin.k/admitted-modules`); UCF §7.6.4 (add the host-export sentence), §7.6.5 (add `:yin.k/host-exports` to the outcome), §7.11 row updated; transport grammar (`requires` slot: the two maps); `yin.vm.linker.dht.md` 7.5.11 amendment reworded; threat-model report is a collab artifact, not edited; known-gaps: Q5 row → landed, R4 row → landed, P2-1 row → closed by step 11.\n16. `bb test:clj` per iteration; at the end `bb test` all three hosts (foreground, one lane set at a time; \"Testing <ns>\" must appear in Node output); kondo; `git diff --check`. Report with counts, mutant kills, old → new addresses. Architect sign-off, then commit `feat(yin.vm.ucf): module pins and host-export pins in requires; lower re-discharges by equal address and profile` and, if the driver seam is separable, a third commit `feat(yin.vm.ucf.holder): admitted-modules config forwarded to the lower`.\n\nCommit split summary: (1) R4 alone, after the P1-1 fix and the rename; (2) carrier + lift + lower + tests + re-mint + docs; (3) optional driver seam if it would otherwise delay (2).\n\nCHANGES-REQUIRED (Part A)\nRULING-READY\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
