{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"tail -42 collab/1793550000000-architect-module-pins-review.report.md; rg -n 'keyed|built|discharge\"'!|requires|check-install-admission|defn lower-task'\"' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '75,160p' src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   - `:yin.k/host-exports {ns/f profile}`: `(= profile (module/host-export-profile (:modules recv) 'ns/f))` → satisfied. Receiver answers another profile → **terminal** `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/kind :host-export-mismatch :yin.k/name ns/f :yin.k/pinned profile :yin.k/held <receiver's>}`. Receiver answers nil (no such export, or the module is absent, or it is linked rather than host) → collected into `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/host-exports {ns/f profile}}` (the `:yin.k/modules {ns nil}` entry will be in the same map when the module is absent).\n   - Receiver's host module exporting **more** than the pin names: satisfied (subset by construction, since only used exports are pinned). Equality is of profile addresses, never of normalised profile maps: the address already covers name, class, arities, effects and host-state.\n   - Carried install children: `:yin.k/admitted-modules {ns address}` equality as today; unlisted → collected into `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {ns carried-address}}`.\n   - Order: terminal mismatches are thrown first (nothing the composition can fetch repairs them), then one collected refusal `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/discovery :complete :yin.k/missing {…}}` with keys present only where something is missing. Zero attaches in every case.\n   - The fetch loop (composition, not this slice) requires only keys of `:yin.k/missing :yin.k/modules` whose pin is non-nil; a nil pin and every `:yin.k/host-exports` entry are composition prerequisites and are not fetched.\n\n5. **Determinism across hosts.** Profile addresses are BLAKE3 content hashes over plain data computed identically on all three hosts (the same mechanism Stage E already pins for primitives); manifest addresses are segment keys. The refusal maps are plain data. Pin T8 in `stage_e_rows_test.cljc`: a `requires` with both maps re-encodes byte-identically and the two terminal refusals and the collected refusal are `=` across JVM, Node and Dart.\n\n6. **Threat-model text amended by this ruling.** §4.2's shape gains `:yin.k/host-exports`; \"whose export profiles equal those the lift recorded\" becomes \"whose profile address for each used export equals the pinned one\"; §4.4's option is renamed `:yin.k/admitted-modules` and its refusal is folded into the collected shape with `:yin.k/discovery :complete`. T4 reads: a nil pin plus `:yin.k/host-exports` is satisfied by a host module answering equal profile addresses for the pinned exports; another profile for a pinned export refuses `:host-export-mismatch`; a missing export is collected as missing; extra exports are ignored.\n\n### B.2 Alternative considered and rejected\n\n\"Refuse nothing for nil pins, document, defer\": `:yin.k/modules {ns nil}` would then only assert \"a host module of this name must exist\", which `resolve-var` already enforces at run time, and skew in `stream`/`cell` profiles between two compositions would still run under R's authority (R6, R8 for the common case). The saving is one map and one lift line; not worth a second re-mint. Rejected.\n\n## Part C: ordered steps for codex round 2\n\nPreconditions: worktree `datomworld-srvm-pins`, the current 13 files uncommitted. `npm ci` and `mise trust` are done there. Per-iteration verification is `bb test:clj`; full three-host `bb test` once at the end, one lane set at a time, foreground only. Read `docs/agents/build-n-test.md` first. No `collab/` path is ever staged.\n\n**Commit 1 (R4, lands alone): fix P1-1, rename P2-2, ledger P2-1.**\n1. `rows.cljc` `install-node`: `response` → `(dissoc response :yin.admit/id :yin.admit/decision :yin.admit/asserters :yin.admit/address)` before the `cbor/encode` check and the row. Delete the restore-side `dissoc` (`rows.cljc:2233-2237` and its comment).\n2. `rows.cljc` `check-install!`: add to the existing `and` of the `:install-response` clause `(not-any? #(= \"yin.admit\" (namespace %)) (filter keyword? (keys response)))`.\n3. Rename `:yin.k/admitted` → `:yin.k/admitted-modules` in `rows.cljc`, `export.cljc`, `rows_support.cljc`, `rows_test.cljc`, `rows_custody_test.cljc`, `export_test.cljc`, `safepoint_harness_test.cljc`.\n4. Tests in `rows_test.cljc` `carried-install-requires-receiver-admission`: keep every assertion; add (a) the decoded wire's root `:install` row slot 3 has none of the four keys, (b) the harness-style relift of the lowered machine is `=` by root to the wire (reuse `canonical-under` or compare the install row), (c) a pack with the four keys spliced into the install row refuses `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response` with zero attaches. In `export_test.cljc`: a frozen parked-installer whose source response carried the sender record rehydrates `:ok` and reproduces the pack byte for byte (this is the P1-1 regression pin).\n5. Mutants (run, record counts, restore): (m1) lift keeps the sender keys → 4(a), 4(b)/export pin fail; (m2) `check-install!` accepts `:yin.admit/*` keys → 4(c) fails; (m3) gate bypass → as before.\n6. Docs (P3-3 list): reword \"dropped on restore\" to \"never carried by the lift; a carried one is refused\", rename the option, add the known-gaps row for P2-1 (holder driver seam, P2) and the P3-2 docstring note. Revisions I-8 wording likewise.\n7. `bb test:clj`, kondo on changed files, `git diff --check`. Report; Architect sign-off; commit `fix(yin.vm.ucf): carried install children need receiver admission; lift never carries sender admission` (format.md convention, no Co-Authored-By).\n\n**Commit 2 (pins carrier + lift + lower + driver seam): the ruling.**\n8. `rows.cljc` lift: in `discharge!` (or a sibling collector over the same `answered?` walk), record for every live registry-answered name the entry: linked → `:yin.k/modules {ns address}`; host → `:yin.k/modules {ns nil}` and `:yin.k/host-exports {ns/f profile}`; nil profile → `:yin.k/non-portable :host-export-profile`. Put both maps into `requires` (`rows.cljc:1687-1689`), sorted, empty maps handled as the existing `requires` keys handle empties.\n9. Encoder/decoder/validator: `requires` is a plain map today, so confirm `check-dependencies!` (`rows.cljc:1918`) still accepts the two extra keys and add the key-count guard for symbol keys as in `built`. Malformed-slot collection: non-map `:yin.k/modules`, non-symbol key, non-string-non-nil value, non-keyword `:yin.k/host-exports` value, unqualified `:yin.k/host-exports` key → `:yin.k/undecodable :requires` (extend the existing kind, no new kind).\n10. `rows.cljc` lower: replace `check-install-admission!` by `check-modules!` per B.1 item 4 (terminal mismatches first, then one collected refusal with `:yin.k/discovery :complete`, zero attaches), same position (after custody, before attach). Delete `check-install-admission!`.\n11. Driver seam (P2-1): `driver/lowered` and the fenced recovery call forward `(:yin.k/admitted-modules (:config state))`; `rehydrate-fenced` already forwards. One driver test with and without the config over a parked-installer checkpoint.\n12. Tests (threat model §7.1, amended): T1 (lift of harness row 17 emits `{:yin.k/modules {host.mod nil} :yin.k/host-exports {host.mod/f <profile>}}`; a DHT-linked fixture emits `{pym.k <address>}`; names answered by `E`, store, prims or module stores emit nothing), T2 (receiver lacking the module: collected refusal, `:discovery :complete`, zero attaches), T3 (linked module at another address: `:module-pin-mismatch` naming both; equal address lowers), T4 (B.1 item 6), T5 (already in commit 1, re-point to the collected shape), T8 (Stage E cross-host row), T9 (layering: `rows.cljc` requires neither `linker.interpreter`, `linker.dht` nor `dao.lease`), T10 (`resolve-var` unchanged). T6/T7 (fetch loop, lease) are composition work, out of this slice; leave their known-gaps rows.\n13. Mutants (run, record, restore): lift records all exports instead of used; lower compares by name presence instead of address; lower accepts a different profile address; lower reports `:incomplete`; attach before `check-modules!`. Each must be killed by a named test.\n14. Fixture re-mint: `rows-checkpoint-v3.txt` and any ledger/Stage E fixture whose `requires` now carries the two maps; record old → new addresses in the report and in `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md` (I-8 completes, dated). C4 scanner pins are untouched (AST-level; see the standing note).\n15. Docs: continuation §2.5 (binding fact travels: the two maps), §7.1 step 6 (records address or host profile), §7.2 dependencies row (module check, three refusal kinds, delete \"the lower does not re-discharge\"), §11 Q5 closed as C with the host-export ruling, Q3 (admitted set is `:yin.k/admitted-modules`); UCF §7.6.4 (add the host-export sentence), §7.6.5 (add `:yin.k/host-exports` to the outcome), §7.11 row updated; transport grammar (`requires` slot: the two maps); `yin.vm.linker.dht.md` 7.5.11 amendment reworded; threat-model report is a collab artifact, not edited; known-gaps: Q5 row → landed, R4 row → landed, P2-1 row → closed by step 11.\n16. `bb test:clj` per iteration; at the end `bb test` all three hosts (foreground, one lane set at a time; \"Testing <ns>\" must appear in Node output); kondo; `git diff --check`. Report with counts, mutant kills, old → new addresses. Architect sign-off, then commit `feat(yin.vm.ucf): module pins and host-export pins in requires; lower re-discharges by equal address and profile` and, if the driver seam is separable, a third commit `feat(yin.vm.ucf.holder): admitted-modules config forwarded to the lower`.\n\nCommit split summary: (1) R4 alone, after the P1-1 fix and the rename; (2) carrier + lift + lower + tests + re-mint + docs; (3) optional driver seam if it would otherwise delay (2).\n\nCHANGES-REQUIRED (Part A)\nRULING-READY\n238:;; count. Members with equal keys form a tie group, postponed and re-keyed\n295:(def ^:private keyed-structural #{:bindings :store :parked-table})\n351:                            (contains? keyed-structural kind)\n461:  \"W1: pre-order in table order; ordered repeated slots in order; keyed\n475:      (contains? keyed-structural kind)\n493:        keyed (mapv (fn [e]\n494:                      ;; One unit per member keyed, so key walks and memo lookups are charged.\n499:                             (sort #(compare-bytes (:bytes (first %1)) (:bytes (first %2))) keyed))]\n618:   in place, keyed rows in key order, a :set or :map as the sorted vector of\n631:      (contains? keyed-structural kind)\n1011:(defn- keyed-node\n1018:  (node :env [(keyed-node :bindings (:yin.k/bindings e) encode) (:yin.k/store-of e)]))\n1024:                 (keyed-node :window (:yin.k/window f) encode) (:yin.k/rd f)]))\n1038:  \"Encode a keyed frame to a frame-rooted version-3 row pack. Values are\n1047:                             (keyed-node :window (:yin.k/window f) encode) k (get-in f [:yin.k/deliver :yin.k/rd])])\n1063:(defn- decode-keyed\n1071:    (cond-> {:yin.k/bindings (decode-keyed bindings decode-value)}\n1079:     :yin.k/env (decode-env e decode-value) :yin.k/window (decode-keyed w decode-value) :yin.k/rd rd}))\n1095:        act? (assoc :yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/env (decode-env e decode-value) :yin.k/window (decode-keyed w decode-value))\n1100:  \"Validate row syntax and hashes, then reshape to the keyed frame.\n1115:        free-env (decode-keyed (nth slots 5) decoded-value)\n1359:   :serve-keyed with [task-path sid] when the caller supplied it.\"\n1363:            keyed (:serve-keyed ctx)]\n1366:        (let [marker (remote/lift-marker (if keyed #(keyed [(:path ctx) sid] %) (:serve! ctx)) h)]\n1595:(defn- discharge!\n1668:        ctx {:m m :serve! serve! :serve-keyed (:serve-keyed opts) :path (or (:path opts) [])\n1684:        _ (discharge! ctx code)\n1689:        requires {:yin.k/cursor-profiles (if (seq (:cells acc)) remote/cursor-profiles #{})\n1693:                          (node :cursor-cells (mapcat identity (:cells acc))) requires code installs waits\n1751:   never travels); :serve-keyed, (f [task-path resource-id] handle), which\n1886:(defn- check-install-admission!\n1914:  \"Step 9, dependency closure: requires and code agree, every segment has\n1920:  (let [[_ _ _ _ _ _ _ module-stores _ _ requires code] (:slots task)]\n1921:    (when-not (and (map? requires) (= (set (:yin.k/segments requires)) (set (keys code))))\n1922:      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :requires {}))\n1923:    (let [trees (:yin.k/trees requires)\n1945:   accept-grant!, ported verbatim, keyed off the root's custody slot c and\n2132:            (built\n2145:                  :set (built n (into #{} (map value) ss) (count ss))\n2146:                  :map (built n (into {} (map (fn [[k x]] [(value k) (value x)])) (partition 2 ss))\n2155:                                                            :yin.k/env (keyed bindings)}\n2160:            (keyed\n2166:                (cond-> (keyed b) (some? store-of) (assoc engine/store-of-key store-of))))\n2171:                        {:type :return :segment (get aliases a) :pc pc :env (env e) :window (keyed w) :rd rd}))\n2179:                  {:segment (get aliases a) :pc pc :env (env e) :window (keyed w) :k (k-of k)\n2240:            fe (keyed free-env)\n2271:(defn lower-task\n2280:   for carried install children (default empty, fail closed). Name-keyed admission\n2303:         (check-install-admission! t opts))\n\n\n(defn link-module\n  \"The `linked` transition's registry update (yin.vm.linker.md sections\n   7.3 and 8.3): `registry` gains the module `manifest` names as the\n   portable encoding of acts 1 to 3 -- `{:manifest m :address a\n   :derivation d :slice {sym encoded} :stores {address snapshot} :cells\n   {cell-id cell} :images {identity image}}` -- never lowered values. `a`\n   is the manifest's own address; `lifted` is the act-1 lift, `{:slice\n   :stores :cells :images}`, the cells being the logical cursor cells its\n   references name (r9) and the images the verified origin images a\n   receiving task attaches.\n   Each receiving task lowers the entry into its own `:bindings`.\"\n  [registry manifest derivation lifted]\n  (assoc-module registry\n                (:yin.module/name manifest)\n                {:manifest manifest,\n                 :address (jing/segment-key manifest),\n                 :derivation derivation,\n                 :slice (:slice lifted),\n                 :stores (:stores lifted),\n                 :cells (:cells lifted),\n                 :images (:images lifted)}))\n\n\n(defn module-entries\n  \"Every `[name entry]` a registry value holds, the module name read back\n   from each entry's manifest.\"\n  [registry]\n  (letfn [(walk\n            [node]\n            (when (map? node)\n              (if (contains? node :manifest)\n                [[(:yin.module/name (:manifest node)) node]]\n                (mapcat walk (vals node)))))]\n    (vec (walk (:modules registry)))))\n\n\n(defn pin-conflict\n  \"The deterministic refusal when receiving `entry` as `module-name`\n   would disagree with a linked manifest's dependency pin. Missing\n   dependencies are permitted; pins are derived from registry manifests.\"\n  [registry module-name entry]\n  (let [linked (filter (fn [[_ e]] (some? (:address e)))\n                       (module-entries registry))\n        existing (keep (fn [[owner e]]\n                         (let [requires (:yin.module/requires (:manifest e))]\n                           (when (and (contains? requires module-name)\n                                      (not= (get requires module-name)\n                                            (:address entry)))\n                             [module-name owner (get requires module-name)\n                              (:address entry)])))\n                       linked)\n        incoming (keep (fn [[name pinned]]\n                         (when-let [held (module-entry (:modules registry) name)]\n                           (when (not= pinned (:address held))\n                             [name module-name pinned (:address held)])))\n                       (:yin.module/requires (:manifest entry)))\n        conflict (first (sort-by (fn [[name owner pinned address]]\n                                   [(str name) (str owner) (str pinned) (str address)])\n                                 (concat existing incoming)))]\n    (when-let [[name _ pinned address] conflict]\n      {:status :refused,\n       :reason :dependency-pin-mismatch,\n       :module module-name,\n       :name name,\n       :pinned pinned,\n       :linked address})))\n\n\n(defn resolve-module\n  \"Get a value from a registry value by dotted symbol path.\n   (resolve-module r 'io)                    → the 'io registry entry\n   (resolve-module r 'io.file-output-stream) → the specific export\"\n  [registry sym]\n  (walk-path (:modules registry) (symbol->path sym)))\n\n\n(defn register-effect-handler\n  \"Return registry with handler-fn installed for effect keyword kw.\n   Handler: (fn [state effect opts] -> {:state s :value v :blocked? bool})\"\n  [registry kw handler-fn]\n  (assoc-in (or registry (empty-registry)) [:effect-handlers kw] handler-fn))\n\n\n(defn get-effect-handler\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
